k = max(-min_pref_rot_k, -S)\n3) Find minO = min_k O_k and collect all k with O_k == minO (candidates).\n4) Among candidates, pick k that minimizes t_k = s[k..] + s[..k] using a rolling-hash-based comparison on u = s+s. Compute the longest common prefix (LCP) of two rotations via double-hash and binary search, then pick the smallest rotation.\n5) Build final answer as: '(' repeated minO, then t_k, then ')' repeated (S + minO).\n6) Print the result.\n\nThis runs in O(n) preprocessing and O(m log n) for comparing m candidate rotations (m ≤ n); using a robust 2-hash (mod 1e9+7 and 1e9+9) ensures practical collision resistance. Memory usage stays within limits for n up to 1e6.\n",
